    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d703">

                <pb facs="0714" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg708"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851W.01/25: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom (Winant) to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-14T18:00:00+01:00">December 14,
                            1942—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7069. The Foreign Office has just informed us that the agreement with General de
                    Gaulle covering the administration of Madagascar is being signed this
                        afternoon.<anchor n="97a" xml:id="d703-f1"/> The agreement we are told
                    preserves “French sovereignty” over the Island and provides for the transfer of
                    civil administration from British to French hands. General Legentilhomme, who
                    has been named High Commissioner, is leaving almost immediately for Madagascar
                    but will confer with General Platt at Nairobi en route concerning details of the
                    turnover. The agreement is to take effect only upon Legentilhomme’s arrival.
                    Provision is made that the British will be responsible for the defense of
                    Madagascar. We have been promised the full text of the agreement which consists
                    of the general terms and three annexes. The first of the latter gives the powers
                    of the British General Officer commanding, the second is a special annex
                    governing operations of the naval base of Diego Suarez and the third covers
                    jurisdiction over British military and non-French nationals. It will be
                    forwarded by air mail.<anchor n="98" xml:id="d703-f2"/> An earlier draft was
                    forwarded with the Embassy’s despatch No. 6313, November 18.<anchor n="99"
                        xml:id="d703-f3"/> A communiqué will be issued this afternoon but the text
                    of the agreement is not being made public.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
